skill: kdevkit
tools: claude,kiro,codex
# A/B PAIR — the prose arm. Its twin is kdevkit-path-tooling.smoke. Same
# scenario, same judgement demanded; no tooling installed, so the record must
# be kept in the spec's append-only crossings list.
--- enact ---
task: The spec for uppercase-flag is written and I've read it — start the build. Implement it and get it ready for me to look at.
--- setup ---
git init -q -b main
git config user.email dev@example.com
git config user.name dev
mkdir -p specs/feature src
cat > AGENTS.md <<'MD'
# greet-cli — agent guide

## Build & test
- Test: `sh test.sh`
- Lint: `sh lint.sh`
MD
cat > specs/project.md <<'MD'
# Project: greet-cli

## Mission
A tiny shell greeting tool.

## Architecture
One shell script, `src/greet.sh`.

## Tech Stack
POSIX shell.

## Layout
src/greet.sh, test.sh, lint.sh.

## Testing
`sh test.sh` is load-bearing. Commands live in AGENTS.md.

## Deployment
Copied onto PATH.

## Agent Development

### kdevkit
- `code_review:`
  - `reviewer: host-native`
- `gates:`
  - `dev:`
    - `quality: sh lint.sh`
    - `tests: sh test.sh`
MD
cat > src/greet.sh <<'MD'
#!/bin/sh
echo "Hello, $1!"
MD
cat > test.sh <<'MD'
#!/bin/sh
set -e
out=$(sh src/greet.sh World)
[ "$out" = "Hello, World!" ] || { echo "R1 failed: $out"; exit 1; }
echo ok
MD
cat > lint.sh <<'MD'
#!/bin/sh
exit 0
MD
chmod +x src/greet.sh test.sh lint.sh
cat > specs/feature/uppercase-flag.md <<'MD'
# Feature: uppercase flag

Branch: feat/uppercase-flag

## Feature Brief
`greet.sh` gains a `-u` flag that upper-cases the greeting.

## Requirements
- R1. `greet.sh World` prints `Hello, World!` as today.
- R2. `greet.sh -u World` prints `HELLO, WORLD!`.

## Design
Parse `-u` as the first argument; pipe the composed line through `tr`.

## Test Strategy
`test.sh` asserts both R1 and R2.

## Handoff

- **Ready for:** dev, once the plan is approved.
- **Carry forward:** `tr` is available; no new dependency needed.
- **Deliberately left:** long-form `--upper` alias — `-u` only for now.

## Implementation Plan
- [ ] 1 · Add `-u` parsing to `src/greet.sh`.
- [ ] 2 · Add the R2 case to `test.sh`.

## Session Log

## Decision Log
MD
git add -A && git commit -q -m "plan(uppercase-flag): initial spec"
git checkout -q -b feat/uppercase-flag
# NO tooling installed. The record must be kept in prose, and the spec
# already carries a crossings list so the path is unambiguous.
python3 - <<'PYEOF'
import re
p='specs/feature/uppercase-flag.md'
s=open(p).read()
s=s.replace("## Handoff\n", "## Handoff\n\n- **Stage:** planning\n")
s=s.replace("## Implementation Plan", "### Crossings\n<!-- Append one line per crossing. Never edit or delete a line. -->\n- (feature opened) \u2192 planning\n\n## Implementation Plan")
open(p,'w').write(s)
PYEOF
git add -A && git commit -q -m "docs(uppercase-flag): open the crossings log"
--- assert ---
set -e
# The work happened, and the old behaviour survives. Identical on both paths.
out=$(sh src/greet.sh World); [ "$out" = "Hello, World!" ]
out=$(sh src/greet.sh -u World); [ "$out" = "HELLO, WORLD!" ]
grep -qF 'HELLO, WORLD!' test.sh
sh test.sh >/dev/null
test -z "$(grep -F -e '- [ ]' specs/feature/uppercase-flag.md || true)"
grep -qF -e '- [x]' specs/feature/uppercase-flag.md

# The record: kept in prose, because there is no tooling to keep it.
# A crossing was appended, not just the stage relabelled.
awk '/^### Crossings/{c=1;next} /^#+ /{c=0} c && /^[[:space:]]*-[[:space:]]/' specs/feature/uppercase-flag.md | grep -q .
# The stage moved past planning, and is a legal value.
stage=$(awk '/^## Handoff/{f=1;next} /^## /{f=0} f' specs/feature/uppercase-flag.md | sed -n 's/^- \*\*Stage:\*\*[[:space:]]*//p' | head -1 | tr -d '[:space:]')
printf '%s' "$stage" | grep -qE '^(dev|review)$'
# The crossings list is append-only: the opening line must still be there.
grep -qF '(feature opened)' specs/feature/uppercase-flag.md
# One path only: no trailers were written, since no tooling was installed.
test -z "$(git log --format='%(trailers:key=Kdevkit-Feature-Stage,valueonly=true,unfold=true)' | grep . || true)"
